## Source, acquisition and exact derivative

The source is [Bag, dynamic angle/color, 3dicons v1](https://3dicons.co/icons/f71a3e-bag?angle=dynamic), by Vijay Verma (@realvjy), published by 3dicons / Overlayz Studio. Its license is CC0 1.0 Universal. Attribution is not required, but source and creator are retained without implying endorsement. Official source-page, library-license and CC0 evidence is retained under `docs/assets/sources/shopping-bag-additional-leads-2026-10-17/`.

The official Download current action requested the color/dynamic/2400-square PNG. The browser download-event wait timed out; the exact new local file was found, its host metadata checked as `https://3dicons.co/`, and its bytes copied unchanged. There is no verified direct PNG CDN URL. The source-page preview was inspected before acquisition and was not used as delivery bytes. FBX/Blender options were observed but no model or animation was acquired.

The original static RGBA PNG is 2400 by 2400, one frame, 2,963,534 bytes, SHA256 `93065262e9028397705eb2ddcaf985942eb3ae81abf21dc5187e331ea5e004da`. Its 46,080,000 decoded bytes exceed the delivery bundle ceiling, so it remains provenance only. The exact accepted derivative uses an alpha-bounds crop with a 16-source-pixel margin and Lanczos reduction to maximum 512 pixels. No contents, handles, materials, colors or new details were invented.

The derivative is 414 by 512, 135,843 encoded bytes and 1,695,744 conservatively accounted decoded bytes. SHA256 is `f978a606233240f896d7255e8f1454df0207194b207d88ef9d5502146c4558bb`. Its proposed raw path is `professional-media/f978a606233240f896d7255e8f1454df0207194b207d88ef9d5502146c4558bb.png`.

## Accepted composition and remaining ambiguity

The original image brief asked for reusable fabric, flexible sides and visible purchases. This acquired image does not demonstrate those properties. The accepted replacement keeps the broad definition, "A bag used to carry purchased items," and shows a plain open retail bag in three-quarter view with a tall solid-sided body, two separate loop handles and a visible opening. It excludes wheels, backpack straps, a closed top, bow, gift tag, tissue and gift-specific decoration. It does not narrow the definition to a material or require contents. Both exact briefs remain in the accepted visual record and later provenance.

The root reviewer inspected the actual original, exact crop and fifteen native comparison states. The tall solid body and paired loops remain distinct from the accepted squat slotted basket through shape and handle construction, not just color. Five Match pair colors, focused and settled, unmatched Match, and full-opacity unmatched/matched Memory preserved the cues; the separate 0.68-alpha stress rows are not the current caller presentation. The native candidate probe passed 534 checks, including exact decoded pixels and scoped-resource lifecycle, with 1,444 protected production files unchanged. These are retained candidate results, not results of a production installation.

The visual/brief acceptance record is `docs/assets/sources/shopping-bag-candidate-review-2026-10-17/visual-review.json`, SHA256 `fa9e40fa7475be0bdd5831ba1907577707fb3557f9f177e7b3f0453df569a97b`. Its source/acquisition/preparation predecessors remain unchanged in their historical states. A generic empty gift bag may share this form; intended shopping use needs context. This is scoped AI picture review, not participant recognition, isolated-picture disambiguation, responsive full-board or browser acceptance.

